risk_description:
Mazda 3: Due to inappropriate software of the powertrain control module (PCM), the automatic idling restart (IR) may fail to restart the engine after idle stopping (i-stop), causing it to stall and increasing the risk of an accident;

Mazda 3 and CX-30: Due to inappropriate software, the powertrain control module (PCM)  may incorrectly judge the half clutch condition as clutch disengaged condition and lower the engine torque to reduce the engine speed to idling condition.
This can cause the engine to stall, increasing the risk of an accident.
